  <div class="home-section">
    <h2>Who trains and what it looks like</h2>
    <p>
      Adults and teenagers from 12–13 train with us, including people with no
      sports background at all. Classes run in the evening, after work and school.
      For your first training a comfortable T-shirt and track pants without hard
      elements are enough — you practice in pairs, guided by the instructor.
      Student grades run 7 kyu: everyone trains in a white belt,
      and the hakama comes at 2 kyu.
      Details on the <a href="/en/first-aikido-training-gdynia.html">first training</a> page.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="home-section">
    <h2>Instructor and school</h2>
    <p>
      Led by Sensei Oskar Szrajer (5 dan). The Polish Aikido Organization continues
      the tradition of <strong>Shihan Fumio Toyoda</strong> (1947–2001) through our
      teacher <strong>Shihan Edward Germanov</strong> (7 dan), directly connected
      to Aikikai Hombu Dojo in Tokyo. More about our teacher:
      <a href="/en/biographies/szrajer.html">Sensei Oskar Szrajer and Sesshinkan Dojo</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="home-section">
    <h2>Top questions before your first training</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Can I start with no experience?</strong> Yes — most people start from zero.</li>
      <li><strong>How much is the first class?</strong> Your first class is free.</li>
      <li><strong>What should I bring?</strong> Track pants without hard elements, a T-shirt, water and a towel.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><a href="/en/faq.html">All answers in the FAQ →</a></p>
  </div>

